        "title": "Spinner text updates in CLI",
        "summary": "Spinner messages updated to include trailing ellipses (e.g., 'Thinking...' instead of 'Thinking'). Logic in `npm-app/src/utils/spinner.ts` modified to remove automatic ellipsis addition. Affects `checkpoint.ts`, `cli.ts`, `client.ts`, `tool-handlers.ts`, and `tool-renderers.ts`.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T13:20:01.036Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the program is busy working on something like thinking of a response or saving your progress, it shows a small message with a spinning indicator next to it. The messages now end with dots like 'Thinking...' instead of just 'Thinking', which is a more standard way to show that activity is ongoing. This change affects the text you see whenever the assistant is processing your request, keeping the wording consistent across different parts of the program. The update is live today.",
